{"name":"Morning Parlour","hex":"#acc0bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"morning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The early part of the day, especially from midnight to noon. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The early part of anything."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good morning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morning"},{"term":"parlour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of parlor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parlour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Morning","blocks":[{"text":"Morning is either the period from sunrise to noon, or the period from midnight to noon. In the first definition it is preceded by the twilight period of dawn, and there are no exact times for when morning begins because it can vary according to one's latitude, and the hours of daytime at each time of year. However, morning strictly ends at noon, when afternoon starts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg/330px-Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morning","wikidata":"Q7722"},{"title":"Parlour","blocks":[{"text":"A parlour is a reception room or public space. In medieval Christian Europe, the \"outer parlour\" was the room where the monks or nuns conducted business with those outside the monastery and the \"inner parlour\" was used for necessary conversation between resident members. In the English-speaking world of the 18th and 19th century, having a parlour room was evidence of social status."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Ca%27_Rezzonico_-_Il_Parlatorio_delle_monache_di_San_Zaccaria_-_Francesco_Guardi.jpg/330px-Ca%27_Rezzonico_-_Il_Parlatorio_delle_monache_di_San_Zaccaria_-_Francesco_Guardi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parlour","wikidata":"Q10550521"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Comet_ison.jpg/500px-Comet_ison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Comet_ison.jpg/1280px-Comet_ison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Comet_ison.jpg/500px-Comet_ison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Comet Ison at dawn, with Mercury at left","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AComet_ison.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg/500px-Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg/1280px-Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg/500px-Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Greek Revival parlour in the Metropolitan Museum of Art","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhotograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Georg_Janny_Salon_im_Makartstil.jpg/500px-Georg_Janny_Salon_im_Makartstil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7